-- title:
--   Direct-sum compatibility of general pinching
-- statement:
--   Let $A,B,C,D$ be arbitrary linear operators on a finite-dimensional complex Hilbert space $\mathcal H$. For any operator $T$, let $\mathcal E_T$ be the Hilbert–Schmidt orthogonal projection onto the commutant of the unital $*$-algebra generated by $T$. Then
--
--   $$\mathcal E_{C\oplus D}(A\oplus B)=\mathcal E_C(A)\oplus\mathcal E_D(B).$$
--
--   The direct sum acts on $\mathcal H\oplus\mathcal H$. For Hermitian $T$, this projection is the sum $\sum_jP_j(\,\cdot\,)P_j$ over distinct spectral eigenvalues, retaining entire degenerate eigenspaces. The formula is useful when passing to classical-label block states.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The literal arbitrary-reference quantifiers use (41): the commutant requires commuting with both $T$ and $T^*$. This extends the Appendix's initial Hermitian setup without a non-Hermitian zero default.
-- source:
--   A New Proof of the Channel Coding Theorem via Hypothesis Testing in Quantum Information Theory, arXiv:quant-ph/0208139v1, PDF p. 8, Lemma 3, (44)

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Intakethird100_P05

